{
 "name": "swa-only-window-hit",
 "description": "A model whose every attention layer is one sliding window (window 8): one KV cache group, so vLLM looks a prefix hit up through SlidingWindowManager (UnitaryKVCacheCoordinator), which needs only the window's blocks. A 10-block pool makes s1 evict the shared prefix's early blocks, so s2's hit is the window's blocks with nulls below them, where a full-attention scan would stop at the first evicted block.",
